# The keys this index needs. Each person's own copy is secrets.env, beside this file: hm clone makes
# it from secrets.env.example, readable only by you. Fill in what you have, and leave the rest empty.
#
# secrets.env is listed in .gitignore, so git never picks it up. Do not rename it, do not
# copy its values into protocol.toml or hm.toml, and do not paste them anywhere that is committed.
# An environment variable of the same name wins over this file.
#
# Claude and OpenAI each take an API key or a subscription: set either one. Where both are set,
# the subscription is used.

# ----- Claude: the worker and frontier tiers on Claude models, and the Claude Code agent -----
# An API key, billed per token:
ANTHROPIC_API_KEY=
# Or a Claude subscription: the token from `claude setup-token`
CLAUDE_CODE_OAUTH_TOKEN=

# ----- OpenAI: the worker and frontier tiers when their provider is "codex", and the Codex agent -----
# An API key, billed per token:
OPENAI_API_KEY=
# Or a ChatGPT subscription: run `codex login` once. Nothing goes in this file: the sign-in is the
# ~/.codex/auth.json it writes, which is found by itself. Only if yours is elsewhere, give its path:
CODEX_AUTH_JSON_PATH=

# ----- the decision tier (Jev, through OpenRouter) -----
OPENROUTER_API_KEY=

# ----- the task store (Hugging Face) -----
# Your own token, with write access to the index's dataset (its owner gives your account the
# write role in their organization). A fine-grained token limited to that dataset is enough.
HF_TOKEN=
